# P11d - Does the input-size limit count a checkpoint restored on a new host?
# @question: With max_transfer_input_mb = 50, a 100 MB spooled checkpoint, and a vacate that forces a restart in a new sandbox: is the restart held for exceeding the input limit (so a checkpoint counts as input), or does it resume? (OSPool access points such as ap40 set MAX_TRANSFER_INPUT_MB = 5000 and don't let users change it.) The container variant also shows whether the osdf:// container image counts.
# @sites: chtc ospool
# @variants: bare
# @triggers: vacate:150
# Timeline: voluntary checkpoint (100 MB) at step 30 and an in-place restart (no new input
# transfer); at ~150 s the vacate: the probe saves again (100 MB) and exits 85, and
# ON_EXIT_OR_EVICT brings that save to spool. The next start, in a new sandbox, must
# transfer the 100 MB checkpoint as part of its input.
max_transfer_input_mb     = 50
checkpoint_exit_code      = 85
transfer_checkpoint_files = ckpt
transfer_output_files     = ckpt, out
when_to_transfer_output   = ON_EXIT_OR_EVICT
stream_output = true
stream_error  = true
request_disk  = 2GB
arguments = $(PROBE_ARGS) --voluntary-exit-at 30 --ckpt-mb 100 --ckpt-files 1 --keep 1 --on-sigterm save85 --total-steps 300
